What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/<bus>-004a/touch_mode
Date:		October 2026
Description:
		Selects the stock volatile touch-controller configuration.
		Accepted values are "finger", "glove" and "stylus". The
		default on driver probe is "finger". Reads return the last
		fully applied mode, followed by a newline. Only root can write.

		A mode change releases all active contacts and capacitive keys,
		writes the complete configuration and calibrates the controller.
		It never updates firmware or nonvolatile settings. Writes while
		the display is blank or the system is suspended return EBUSY.
		Unknown values return EINVAL.

		An incomplete configuration write, IRQ message read failure or
		controller reset/config fault stops touch reporting. Reads then return EIO; writing a
		valid mode while awake reapplies the entire configuration.
		A failed sleep/wake transition also stops reporting, but retains
		a completed configuration; writing its mode retries scanning.
		After a completed sleep, wake performs the stock soft reset and
		100ms wait, then restores the selected volatile configuration.
		Successful writes return the supplied byte count.
